
Azure Kusto Query Language (KQL) Exception Tracking Report
1. KQL Investigation Queries
Query 1: Filter Failing Requests with Error Details
requests
| where timestamp >= ago(24h)
| where success == false
| project timestamp, id, name, resultCode, duration, cloud_RoleName, operation_Id, user_AuthenticatedId
| order by timestamp asc


This query filters unsuccessful requests from the last 24 hours and displays the request name, result code, duration, service name, operation ID, and affected user.

Query 2: Correlate Requests with Exceptions Using Join
requests
| where timestamp >= ago(24h)
| where success == false
| join kind=inner (
    exceptions
    | where timestamp >= ago(24h)
    | project operation_Id, ExceptionType=type, MethodName=method,
              ExceptionMessage=message, handledAt, severityLevel
) on operation_Id
| project timestamp, operation_Id, RequestName=name, resultCode,
          duration, cloud_RoleName, ExceptionType, MethodName,
          ExceptionMessage, handledAt, severityLevel
| order by timestamp asc


This query performs an inner join using operation_Id. It connects each failed request with the corresponding exception.

Query 3: Dependency Failure Rate and Duration Mapping
dependencies
| where timestamp >= ago(24h)
| summarize
    TotalCalls=count(),
    FailedCalls=countif(success == false),
    FailureRate=round(100.0 * countif(success == false) / count(), 2),
    AverageDurationMs=round(avg(duration), 2)
    by target, type
| extend OperationalHealth=case(
    FailureRate >= 50, "Critical",
    FailureRate > 0, "Degraded",
    "Healthy"
)
| order by FailureRate desc


This query groups dependencies by target and type, calculates total calls, failed calls, failure percentage, average duration, and operational health.

Query 4: Time-Series Error Render
requests
| where timestamp >= ago(24h)
| where success == false
| summarize ErrorCount=count() by bin(timestamp, 5m), cloud_RoleName
| render timechart


This query displays failed requests as a time-series chart using five-minute intervals.

